  "verdict": "CONDITIONING DOES NOT RECOVER THE COLLAPSE: the best arm (desc) moves cross-metal AUC by -0.0215 (paired bootstrap 95% CI [-0.0565, +0.0157], Holm p=1.0000); the cross-metal collapse is intrinsic to the metal axis, not an artefact of an unconditioned scorer.",
  "caveats": [
    "The token arm's held-out metal embedding is never trained in LOMO, so it is a random vector at test time — the arm bounds what an UNLEARNED token can do, not what a learned one could.",
    "The desc arm's descriptors are public periodic-table constants read from molmetal/data/transition_metals_30.csv; no label information crosses the split.  They encode periodic position (atomic number, group, period), formal oxidation state, a d-count proxy and a coordination-geometry one-hot — not ligand-field or redox potentials.",
    "Rh (n=51), Os (n=36) and Re (n=74) test folds are small; per-metal deltas on those cells carry large variance.",
    "GPU bf16 training is not bit-reproducible (~0.01-0.03 per-seed AUC drift), which is why the baseline arm is re-run in-session and the test is paired rather than against the PA3 canonical directly."
  ],
  "honest_framing_note": "Every number is MEASURED from the three arm reports on disk; the verdict and contributes_method flag are derived from the bootstrap CI and the Holm-adjusted p, not asserted."
